# Licence

Three kinds of material live in this repository, under three different terms.
They are separated here because collapsing them into one licence would either
over-claim or under-grant.

---

## 1. The architecture — public domain

The concepts, grammars, protocols, formats and operating-system designs
described in this repository and in the book series are dedicated to the public
domain, irrevocably, as published. Anyone may use them. No permission is
required. No fee will ever be charged. No patent claim will be made, now or in
the future, by the author or by anyone acting on his behalf.

The governing statement is **[THIS_ARCHITECTURE_IS_YOURS.md](THIS_ARCHITECTURE_IS_YOURS.md)**.
Where this summary and that document differ, that document governs.

## 2. Reference implementation code — Apache 2.0

Any source code in this repository — now or added later — is released under the
Apache License, Version 2.0. You may use, modify and redistribute it, including
commercially, subject to the standard Apache 2.0 terms, which include a patent
peace clause.

## 3. The books and prose — © James Lee Stäkelum

The book series and the written argument are copyrighted in the usual way. That
covers the PDF in `books/` and the prose of the essays, including
`THE_SYNAPSE.md`.

You may re-express the architecture in your own words, write your own
implementations, and build products on it, without citing the books. You may
not reproduce the book text itself.

---

## In practice

| You want to | Allowed |
|---|---|
| Build a system on this architecture | Yes — no permission, no fee |
| Re-implement it in any language | Yes |
| Use it commercially | Yes |
| Fork the specification and run your own consensus | Yes — this is the intent |
| Redistribute the book PDF or its text | No — copyrighted prose |
| Redistribute the specification text as your own | No — but re-expressing the ideas is fine |

Attribution is welcome and not required, with one exception: the prose.
